:46:59-07:00","id":257788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257779#post257779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i hope that in the 3ed edition the charm trees will be more smooth, not something like starting with ability3 essence2 requirements</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I've understood, Exalts will no longer automatically have Essence 2 from the start, so it should be more smooth in that regard at least. I wonder if we'll actually see any Ability 1, Essence 1 Charms beyond Excellencies, though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T19:51:52-07:00","id":257796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257786#post257786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...cut Lunars from the gameline, and give Sidereals two hardbacks' worth of Charms and Martial Arts and Sorcery and Evocations? Gotcha!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you're willing to make the difficult decision. I hope you\u2019re ready for when Tornado Wolf finds you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T19:55:34-07:00","id":257802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257796#post257796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm glad you're willing to make the difficult decision. I hope you\u2019re ready for when Tornado Wolf finds you.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not for nothing that I have spent dozens of years mastering the Petting Hand Technique!<br /> <br /> (one time I tried to pet an alligator and that was a bad decision)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T20:02:19-07:00","id":257808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257768#post257768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Potential problem: the general response I've found is &quot;if it's not the original Charms from 1e, right down to the flavour text, it's not really Sidereals&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> I mean... good luck, and as far as I'm concerned sacred cows go well with BBQ sauce, but... this will be another fustercluck.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really don't think that sentiment is as widespread as it may seem. I mean, people are definitely married to a lot of the concepts introduced by the 1e charmset, but 2e's presentation was so absolutely horrendous that I think a competent-yet-different set will not provoke endless ire.<br /> <br /> (It will certainly provoke some ire, because every last tiny motherfucking element of every edition of Exalted has a rabid fan SOMEWHERE, but I don't think that's substantively different from the twenty thousand Lunars fans who will swear eternal enmity if Shapeshifting either is or is not the primary focus of the splat in 3e.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T20:24:48-07:00","id":257814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257788#post257788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I've understood, Exalts will no longer automatically have Essence 2 from the start, so it should be more smooth in that regard at least. I wonder if we'll actually see any Ability 1, Essence 1 Charms beyond Excellencies, though</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see the case against, though I could easily see it happening. I mean, obviously 1 dot in a skill isn't anything world-shaking, but it does indicate that one has developed oneself in that area beyond the assumed default of 0. In principle, that's 5 levels of advancement beyond the baseline you've got to work with when building a Charmset.<br /> <br /> Hmm. Spoilering, as I abandon all pretense that I'm not on a tangent for a few sentences: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I wonder if one of the difficulties of an Attribute-based Charmset is that (at least in 1e and 2e) 2-dots is already the baseline, so you functionally only have 3 levels of development beyond &quot;normal&quot; to build the set. I remember Holden once said a Charmset's structural thesis is harder to make for an Attribute-based one than for an Ability-based one, unless using a very different approach to &quot;cheat&quot; like Alchemicals did. Having fewer levels above the baseline could be one factor.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T20:34:11-07:00","id":257818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257462#post257462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Auspicious Prospects doesn't actually do anything</i>. In my last game we made it a way to bleed off Paradox without having to sit on your ass for days at a time. But still!<br /> <br /> Embracing Life Method is useless for any actual investigation that isn't gimmicky bullshit like finding out about the Great Curse. The time needed, even if you go early, is too great.<br /> <br /> Sidereal Shell Games was moderately broken in its original incarnation but got pretty defanged in the errata. I wouldn't say it's worthless to take it, but it's definitely not as useful as it was.<br /> <br /> There's no fucking reason at all for Murder Moving Fingers Dance to be a Martial Arts Charm. Except closed charmset bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I feel sometimes like I'm the only one that understands Auspicious Prospects is a weal or woe thing for whatever purview you bought the Charm for. I'd definitely not go so far to say it doesn't do anything, and at least to me it's a fairly common sense reading of the Charm.<br /> <br /> A lot of Sidereal stuff is that way IMO but the wider fandom opinion seems to be that without (utterly unnecessary) exacting mechanical language Charms don't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","name":"UltraFennec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar748_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T20:47:28-07:00","id":257828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257788#post257788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I've understood, Exalts will no longer automatically have Essence 2 from the start, so it should be more smooth in that regard at least. I wonder if we'll actually see any Ability 1, Essence 1 Charms beyond Excellencies, though</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but not as many as the Ability 2/Essence 1 or Ability 3/Essence 1 Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T22:50:50-07:00","id":257901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257604#post257604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't really care for the idea of the Scarlet Empress having been given a super-Destiny anymore, but when I did I liked to imagine that Chejop despondently looked out over advancing armies of Fair Folk and planted a prayer strip with the question &quot;how do I fix this?&quot;, and coming back five days later to find leaves with little factoids about a certain Dragon Blooded officer, as well as a certain trinket that he didn't understand but during his meeting with the Empress proved critical with convincing her that he was on the level.<br /> <br /> That's probably only slightly lower down than the Great Curse, but I still think the basic outline of it is both useful and interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Embracing Life Method is great as a plot point generator or as a way to hit the GM and say &quot;Okay, we're stumped, where should we go next?&quot; It's next to useless in an actual investigation, because in the five days you have to wait for it to sprout you'd get the same or better results just by beating feet.<br /> <br /> I've never been in the school of thought that says that you should only ever bother to do rolls you can enhance with Charms, hell my last campaign I made two or three times the unenhanced rolls as the other players, but if I'm buying a Charm that's supposed to help with investigation, then, ya'know, I want it to help with investigation.<br /> <br /> I love Jenna Moran, don't get me wrong, but I think I'm at the point where I'm willing to sacrifice some of her trademark weirdness so that Sidereals don't wind up with a charmset (a closed charmset, remember) that's half gimmicky bullshit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>UltraFennec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257818#post257818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel sometimes like I'm the only one that understands Auspicious Prospects is a weal or woe thing for whatever purview you bought the Charm for. I'd definitely not go so far to say it doesn't do anything, and at least to me it's a fairly common sense reading of the Charm.<br /> <br /> A lot of Sidereal stuff is that way IMO but the wider fandom opinion seems to be that without (utterly unnecessary) exacting mechanical language Charms don't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Jupiter Approves*&quot; popping up on my UI doesn't actually help me, though, particularly since we have the typical depiction of the Maidens being &quot;Who the fuck knows why they do anything?&quot; <br /> <br /> And yes, for forty fucking XP to buy all five versions of the Charm instead of something <i>sensible</i> like buying it once and then buying the other four purviews for one XP each, I expect some kind of goddamn concrete benefit out of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257558#post257558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If only we had some kind of opportunity to rewrite the Sidereal Charmset from first principles, drawing inspiration from everything cool about them and marrying them to new, better mechanics while correcting the errors of the past. Nah, that's pretty unlikely.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, TDO, I'm very very conflicted on 3e Sidereals.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, you guys wrote Sidereal Firearms and Sidereal Drive, both of which I absolutely love. Celestial Drifter's Panoply is goddamn fantastic and the sort of effect I think Sidereals need more of, particularly in comparison to that shitty ass Craft Charm whose name I can't recall at the moment (and my books are sitting in boxes because IKEA is dragging their feet on getting me my goddamn bookcases).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, you guys wrote Simple Astrology, which I loathe with the burning heat of ten thousand suns going nova inside an industrial furnace.<br /> <br /> So I really don't know if I should be hopeful or wary of 3e Sidereals. :/<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">*Morrigan, of course, disapproves</span><br /> <br /> (This post is dedicated to my cat, who decided to walk over my keyboard when it was 3/4 finished and reload the page.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T23:08:17-07:00","id":257905,"title":"","content":"Given the blade focused Martial Arts Styles we're getting in the Core, I'm not sure Violet Bier of Sorrows Style is necessary at all at this point. Were it up to me, Sids would get Thrown Shadow conceptually integrated as their native Brawl tree, and then get Sidereal Styles (ontop of the classic three) associated with each Department of the Bureau of Destiny - so &quot;Sapphire Veil of Passion&quot; for the Cerulean Lute, and whatever needs to be preserved from Endings Style can come over into a more esoteric Sidereal style associated with the Violet Bier.<br /> <br /> In addition - and I cannot stress the point enough - MAKE GREATER ASTROLOGY CHARMS A DEFAULT PART OF THE SETTING.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T23:21:15-07:00","id":257928,"title":"","content":"I kinda wonder if anybody here like Unweaving Method, I mean, perfect aggravated attack are nice, and the fluff is awesome too, but since the cost is so high it seem like you can only use the charm two or three times per battle at most.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257741#post257741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is up with that girl's bodyshape?</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean Iron Siaka ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 09-16-2014, 02:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T23:28:58-07:00","id":257932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257901#post257901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, you guys wrote Simple Astrology, which I loathe with the burning heat of ten thousand suns going nova inside an industrial furnace.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple Astrology was a patch to work around the complexities of a system that wasn't fun for a lot of players. It's not the kind of thing we're going to have to use when we have the opportunity to build the system from the ground up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T23:40:53-07:00","id":257939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257901#post257901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love Jenna Moran, don't get me wrong, but I think I'm at the point where I'm willing to sacrifice some of her trademark weirdness so that Sidereals don't wind up with a charmset (a closed charmset, remember) that's half gimmicky bullshit.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This, very much. I love the idea of Sidereals, the themes they're supposed to have, but most of their charms feel like spells: random effects that don't have much to do with being a secret master who controls fate itself. I think Throne Shadow is my favourite Sid charm tree, and its the only one that's nothing to do with 1st ed, because it's actually a martial art about being a secret master. Whereas most Sidereal charms are not, at all. They're just &quot;we're the wacky esoteric exalts, but that seems pretty powerful, so here's a bunch of random holes in the charmset that can't be fixed so suck it up.&quot;<br /> Like spells, a lot of the effects are really fun and cool (I've got your name! Na-na-na-na, got your name!) but a proper charm set they do not make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T23:42:18-07:00","id":257940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257901#post257901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love Jenna Moran, don't get me wrong, but I think I'm at the point where I'm willing to sacrifice some of her trademark weirdness so that Sidereals don't wind up with a charmset (a closed charmset, remember) that's half gimmicky bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realize the closed charmset was Grabowski's decision, not Jenna's?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T01:10:22-07:00","id":257974,"title":"","content":"I think in the past, I've been less critical of Sidereal Charms than I could've been - partly because Jenna Moran is awesome, so Sidereal Charms are pretty awesome and shiny, in her characteristically conceptually novel way. And they do hit the Sidereal inspirations really well. <br /> <br /> Nonetheless:<br /> <br /> 1) Agree that they could do with more iconic Charms that focus on how they operate through foresight and subtle influence over the world that can look like good fortune or chance (or even talent), while keeping interesting choices and restrictions, and that their Charms maybe could feel less like sorcery (like Embracing Life Method feels a lot like a magician doing a spell, not so much like using skill over Fate's essence and nature).<br /> <br /> Their default seems supposed to be fairly subtle, not overt sorcerors who can operate in quite a disguised manner. Their brief to be ostentatiously sorcerous bureaucratic angels of Chinese heaven has to be handled with their brief to be covert seers.<br /> <br /> I see that you can view this to be like kung fu and imperial agent styled version of the Traveller in Black - at first they're this innocuous little man and everything's a bit odd, then sooner or later it become obvious they're throwing down world shaping magic to reaffirm order's hold against chaos. I just have this feeling they feel a bit like sorcerors more than having power over Fate sometimes.<br /> <br /> 2) I think also that when you look at the Caste summaries of the Sidereals, they are substantially heavy on information there about how the Sidereals helped to build the First Age civilization, rebuild the world in the wake of the Great Contagion, facilitate the Usurpation in unique Caste appropriate ways, etc.<br /> <br /> Rebuilding this civilization is not, exactly, what 3e games are totally focused on. Yet, I feel like their existing set kind of isn't strong on any feeling of how they would go about this. <br /> <br /> Like the Chosen of Battles write up says &quot;The Shieldbearers advised the Dawn Caste generals ... using the Chosen's visions of the future to place troops with an uncanny wisdom&quot;. Are the &quot;Battle Plan&quot; Charms, or Battles Charms in general, sufficient to model this well? They seem good at forcing people to do what they want, and at uncanny magical blessings on the battlefield but not very useful at actually advising people.<br /> <br /> Or for Serenity, &quot;During the First Age, the Chosen of Serenity advised the Solar Deliberative on the health and well-being of Creation's millions of mortals... examin(ing) the Loom of Fate for outbreaks of misfortune and spreading dissatisfaction ... wove destinies of joy to bless the efforts to restore harmony&quot;.<br /> <br /> How well do the Secrets Charms support the idea of them managing the process of discovery and occlusion of knowledge their Caste summary provides? Which trees of their actually feel appropriate in helping them do this? Etc.<br /> <br /> Their magic (whether Charms or astrology) should surely actually support this stuff, as a primary purpose?<br /> <br /> It feels like each tree is hung up on making a strong, defining statement (Ride is about using people to get to where you're going, etc.), which is awesomely cool, and leaving the audience a little puzzled about how to achieve some goals (solving which puzzle is supposed to be part of their fun), but each tree sometimes seems to be fairly loosely informed by what the Sidereals are actually doing in changing and reshaping the world and to what purpose they do so.<br /> <br /> I think I mostly have some echo of Wizard of Oz's comment here, except I think it's better to focus on their ability to achieve the Caste goals through their power to have foresight, to advise, and to bless and curse. With focusing on them as generic secret masters without really describing how this links to Caste goals, I think there's already a lot of fans who are hostile to them as people who secretly control and dominate others while really achieving nothing, and that's not really something to emphasise further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T02:06:22-07:00","id":257987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257940#post257940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do realize the closed charmset was Grabowski's decision, not Jenna's?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that Holden's also said repeatedly it's going to stay. Which is a decision I'm all for. It's one of the most interesting aspects of sidereals.<br /> <br /> Also, Ox-body has always been useless. It's one of the charms I wish sidereals just didn't have or was redone in a way that they could actually see themselves purchasing it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T02:31:10-07:00","id":257988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257558#post257558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If only we had some kind of opportunity to rewrite the Sidereal Charmset from first principles, drawing inspiration from everything cool about them and marrying them to new, better mechanics while correcting the errors of the past. Nah, that's pretty unlikely.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Personally I'm not worried about the mechanical quality of charms you will develop.<br /> <br /> But there are deep patterns in the charm trees (yeah when it comes to sids, patterns are always involved somewhere) they may very well linger in 3rd ed. And it is the narrowing of the trees theme to the associated maiden's purview.<br /> <br /> Most people think the opposite because they see a few charms mechanically out of the core themes of a tree, like a charm that not only helps resist poison but also redirects it to an enemy in resistance.<br /> <br /> The truth is sids charms, contrary to solars, are mainly tied to the maiden's purview and very loosely tied to the ability. And this is where the problem starts :<br /> 25 abilities cover more efficiently a wider area of skills and crafts than the 5 maiden's purviews, and what makes things worse is that charms have a &quot;double allegiance&quot; to both the maiden as a general theme and to the ability as a means of expression of the power, though in a few cases it can be a very loose tie.<br /> <br /> The basic idea is great, both for fluff and as a concept, but one of the consequences are :<br /> the medicine charm tree, being focused on the ending aspect, has almost no real healing power, and the pinacle charm has to really stretch the concept of ending (finding a soon-to-die spirit and make a deal where he gives healing to avoid his fate) to do the bloody job. Making sids one of the most laughable physicians/surgeons and possibly less qualified than terrestrials and other lesser essence users it it weren't for their TN excellency.<br /> <br /> there is no &quot;ammo&quot; charm for thrown, because it doesn't fit travels. Instead (in 2.5) you use on of travel's sub theme to send a &quot;messenger&quot; represent the weapon while keeping the actual weapon in your hand, while similarly archery could not have a similar effect.<br /> <br /> <b>So to clarify my wish for 3rd ed :</b><br /> <br /> It would be really nice to add a few charms in each tree that would express the view of the 4 other maidens about that particular ability, even if you have to leave them on a secondary tree not related to the pinacle charm and the associated scripture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T02:41:01-07:00","id":257991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257905#post257905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition - and I cannot stress the point enough - MAKE GREATER ASTROLOGY CHARMS A DEFAULT PART OF THE SETTING.</div> </div> </div> </div>I seem to recall indications that Greater Astrology charms were mostly considered part of the patch to make Sidereals a playable splat again however the Paradox cost proved useful in giving certain effects a steep cost that was more difficult to recover than willpower or health levels but didn't represent a permanent loss of traits so players would agonise over if they wanted to use them or not.<br /> <br /> 3e has more palatable ways of providing great power in limited doses without &quot;the spiders will eat you&quot; but for certain forbidden techniques it could be very thematic. I've had interesting ideas about a Rakan Thulio boss fight where he can keep deferring his death at the PCs' hands but when he hits 10 Paradox he's out of luck and out of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T03:18:55-07:00","id":257997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257784#post257784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the 1e Sidereal Charmset was a fucking <i>poem</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I can't tell if this is praise or criticism...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T03:21:15-07:00","id":257999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257940#post257940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do realize the closed charmset was Grabowski's decision, not Jenna's?</div> </div> </div> </div>In fairness to Coik, I think his point isn't about the closed set itself, but that it exacerbates the idea that valuable limited space is taken up by Charms that are more whimsical than useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T07:09:21-07:00","id":258090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257932#post257932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple Astrology was a patch to work around the complexities of a system that wasn't fun for a lot of players. It's not the kind of thing we're going to have to use when we have the opportunity to build the system from the ground up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the issue with Simple Astrology for me was that it seemed to address the wrong issue. The number of rolls was never an issue for me, particularly once 2e rolled around and Sidereals got general Excellencies. Based on the fact that Astrology forces you to at least moderately specialize in it to get anything done at all (which, at minimum, I feel is moderate investment in Performance, Second Performance Excellency or Serenity caste, and at least a two dot specialty in Sidereal Astrology), and that Astrology takes so goddamn long to do <i>anything</i> that you can basically assume you have infinite Essence available to throw at it...well, you can pretty much obviate the Prayer roll. More than likely by Essence 3 and definitely by Essence 4 (which Sidereals were all highly motivated to get, since it opened up all non-SMA Charms). You could pretty much just assume a +1 or +2 on the Effect roll, depending on how much you've invested in Performance.<br /> <br /> On the other claw, Simple Astrology gave out Paradox, the <i>real</i> problem with Astrology, like it was goddamn candy and Simple Astrology was Willie Wonka on Halloween.<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, I'd love it if 3e gave you a reason to play Journeys or Battles. Seriously don't think I've ever seen anyone take those castes...it's either Serenity for the free Performance Excellency (thereby freeing up a Charm pick), or Secrets/Endings for the free Favored on one of Sidereals' godskills. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You do realize the closed charmset was Grabowski's decision, not Jenna's? </div> </div> </div>Isator pretty much got what I was going for...Jenna's Charms are awesome, but when The Book Says(tm) that you only get three Investigation Charms ever unless you make a Martial Art centered around punching witnesses and evidence, it puts space at a much greater premium, particularly since it makes it much harder to walk up to a GM and be all &quot;I have a great new Sidereal Investigation Charm! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> &quot; and they come back with &quot;Well, The Book Says(tm) that you only get three Investigation Charms ever...&quot;<br /> <br /> Now I'll grant this is from the perspective of 1e/2e, where the game mechanics hated you, the player, personally and was out to murderlize you as quickly, brutally and efficiently as possible. Maybe 3e you have room for a few flavor Charms without having to sit and weigh if it's the most mechanically efficient use of your time and XP...I dunno, I haven't seen it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257987#post257987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Ox-body has always been useless. It's one of the charms I wish sidereals just didn't have or was redone in a way that they could actually see themselves purchasing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, don't get me started on Ox-Body. I still have the occasional flashback to the thread on the old forums... *shudder*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257991#post257991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to recall indications that Greater Astrology charms were mostly considered part of the patch to make Sidereals a playable splat again however the Paradox cost proved useful in giving certain effects a steep cost that was more difficult to recover than willpower or health levels but didn't represent a permanent loss of traits so players would agonise over if they wanted to use them or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Greater Astrology and Throne Shadow were both ways to give Sidereals new Charms without giving Sidereals new Charms, because closed Charmset so obviously Sidereals couldn't be given new Charms, right?<br /> <br /> I'd have to troll through the What We Know, but I'm pretty sure I remember hatewheel stating that the philosophy going forward will be that, if Sidereals need Charms for a mechanical need that pops up later in the game's lifecycle, they'll just go ahead and add them to the base trees with the &quot;Of course it's always been there&quot; wink and a nod.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T07:32:21-07:00","id":258118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257901#post257901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Embracing Life Method is great as a plot point generator or as a way to hit the GM and say &quot;Okay, we're stumped, where should we go next?&quot; It's next to useless in an actual investigation, because in the five days you have to wait for it to sprout you'd get the same or better results just by beating feet.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it's part of Investigation, I don't view Embracing Life Method as a method for fact finding so much as a means for laying the ground work of certain long term plans.<br /> <br /> Although even in the area of fact-finding, it's good for covering the bases of Efficient Secretary Technique vis a vis &quot;investigating things you have absolutely no proximity to&quot;. I think one area Sidereal Charms should and do focus on is the idea of them multi-tasking and delegating, and most of their Investigation Charms seem to elegantly incorporate both to me. If you're busy managing certain matters pertaining to military preparation in the Realm, and really need to have a look into some of the plans and actions of the Bull of the North, but are wholly unable to because he's too far away and you can't afford to leave what you're overseeing at the moment, asking nature spirits to prophetically gather information for you can probably be pretty valuable. The five day waiting period isn't something you spend twiddling your thumbs during, it's a deadline for coordination; you really want to make sure the armies are prepared to roll out at the same moment as you gather a bunch of auspicious data points regarding Kaneko's campaign. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T08:39:35-07:00","id":258181,"title":"","content":"I kinda hope that Astrology will be robust and smooth, and, more importantly, that <i>you can use it for information gathering.</i> And you should be able to use it anywhere, with direct access to the Loom (or a ?Getimian?) gives you a boost - you should be able to glance at how the steam from your tea swirls in the air before dispersing to get an update on a battle 100 miles away.<br /> <br /> Actually, just information gathering (and the ability to better act on that information) would be a great focus; secret masters and advisers work <i>so much better</i> when they actually know what's going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T10:06:52-07:00","id":258251,"title":"","content":"Ever since I first read it, I have loved <b>Avoiding the Truth Technique</b>....in theory.<br /> <br /> After I learned a bit more about how social combat and stunting works, however, I realized something: it does literally nothing. You have to stunt your truth-that-is-to-be-seen-as-a-lie to justify using the Charm. But if you just roll a Manipulation check and stunt your social attack as, &quot;I tell him the truth, but in such a way that it sounds preposterous and he thinks I'm either lying or utterly addled, so will dismiss what I'm saying as wholly fictitious,&quot; you get the same effect, but without spending motes and possibly regaining some!<br /> <br /> Avoiding the Truth Technique doesn't even add dice to the roll, not that it would be all that great if it did, because <i>excellencies</i> do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T10:26:23-07:00","id":258271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257997#post257997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't tell if this is praise or criticism...</div> </div> </div> </div>? Given the context, I'm having trouble parsing what Vance said as criticism. Could you clarify how you see it reading that way?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T10:28:07-07:00","id":258275,"title":"","content":"I know that I'm many years late to the party but even though it's as relevant as whining about the interface in Wordperfect I'd like to share my feeligns on Blade of the battle maiden in second edition.<br /> <br /> It was messed up in the storytellers companion. Everyone immediately saw it was messed up. Folks spent years complaining about how it was messed up and when the Siderial book came out.. the charm was unchanged. How could the developers and writers have missed the years of annoyance that preceded the book? Someone had to copy paste that charm and decide, &quot;No, the guy/gal who wrote the storyteller's companion got this right. It's the people who've actually been playing the game for the past few years who don't get it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Arrrgh!!<br /> <br /> Thank you for reading. I actually do feel better now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T10:35:40-07:00","id":258278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you just roll a Manipulation check and stunt your social attack as, &quot;I tell him the truth, but in such a way that it sounds preposterous and he thinks I'm either lying or utterly addled, so will dismiss what I'm saying as wholly fictitious,&quot; you get the same effect, but without spending motes and possibly regaining some!</div> </div> </div> </div> Avoiding the Truth Technique means you tell the truth in a manner that sounds absolutely plausible and reasonable, and the person thinks you're lying anyway. Among other things, that's the sort of thing that is liable to undermine other people's confidence in the person, more than them dismissing something that actually sounded outlandish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T11:38:51-07:00","id":258330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=258271#post258271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">? Given the context, I'm having trouble parsing what Vance said as criticism. Could you clarify how you see it reading that way?</div> </div> </div> </div>Either it is both a functional Charmset AND a poem at the same time (good) or it is ONLY a poem without being a functional Charmset (bad). These are the two possible readings of Vance's statement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T12:11:56-07:00","id":258354,"title":"","content":"A friend was going to run a Sidereal game at one point, and at the time Orichalcum Chef was making its rounds on the Forums, so I came up with a really fun Chosen of Serenity that used it. Not wanting to sink all my starting charms into MA, I figured I'd see how useful the Craft charms would be to the character.<br /> <br /> Apparently, at least in 2E, unless you're crafting Artifacts, the only useful charms are the Excellencies. He ended up being mostly MA and Socialize/Presence","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T12:15:10-07:00","id":258357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=258278#post258278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Avoiding the Truth Technique means you tell the truth in a manner that sounds absolutely plausible and reasonable, and the person thinks you're lying anyway. Among other things, that's the sort of thing that is liable to undermine other people's confidence in the person, more than them dismissing something that actually sounded outlandish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, nothing that can't be done with a Manipulation+Perform check. You tell the truth in a way that sounds a lie to your target specifically undermining the rest of our audience's confidence in him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T13:47:07-07:00","id":258424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257604#post257604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't really care for the idea of the Scarlet Empress having been given a super-Destiny anymore, but when I did I liked to imagine that Chejop despondently looked out over advancing armies of Fair Folk and planted a prayer strip with the question &quot;how do I fix this?&quot;, and coming back five days later to find leaves with little factoids about a certain Dragon Blooded officer, as well as a certain trinket that he didn't understand but during his meeting with the Empress proved critical with convincing her that he was on the level.<br /> <br /> That's probably only slightly lower down than the Great Curse, but I still think the basic outline of it is both useful and interesting.<br /> <br /> I mean, if a Sidereal had a question of &quot;how can I take down the Walker in Darkness&quot;, he might get a leaf saying &quot;did you know that Jiurnan Nightwarden Exalted while trying to save an undead woman being sent to serve as a consort to the Warden?&quot; That's a relevant detail that one is unlikely to pick up elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, God, no! That meglomaniacal asshat already considers himself the One True Holy Omniscient and Omnipotent God of Creation - don't go just straight out making him right! I have no problem with the basic use of the Charm in that narrative, but at least make it Chuckles McTubbybelly the Random Sidereal. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Mod edit, went too far with the unnecessary sexual language and imagery, please refrain from doing so in the future. Darksider</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 09-16-2014, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1651-phalamir","name":"phalamir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T13:49:25-07:00","id":258425,"title":"","content":"I really hope the closed Charmset primarily filled with weird gimmicky stuff remains a thing. I mean, it'd be nice for it to be <i>useful</i> weird gimmicky stuff, but honestly if it came down to one or the other I'd personally choose to keep the &quot;saving the world with some pocket lint, three feet of twine and a spork&quot; thing over having a well-rounded Charmset with nary a second thought.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*braces for imminent stabbing*</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/471-cenobite451","name":"Cenobite451","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar471_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T14:00:49-07:00","id":258440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cenobite451</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=258425#post258425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really hope the closed Charmset primarily filled with weird gimmicky stuff remains a thing. I mean, it'd be nice for it to be <i>useful</i> weird gimmicky stuff, but honestly if it came down to one or the other I'd personally choose to keep the &quot;saving the world with some pocket lint, three feet of twine and a spork&quot; thing over having a well-rounded Charmset with nary a second thought.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*braces for imminent stabbing*</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm with you!<br /> <br /> Not that I don't have complete faith in TDO, John and Holden, but I've played Sidereals doggedly through an entire goddamn broken edition for a reason. There are plenty of more effective options; it is not that which calls to fans of Sidereals.<br /> <br /> But I'll tell you what- I'm all for <i>more</i> charms. Of all the complaints I see in this thread, 'I really would like to have a few more Investigation charms' really strikes closest to home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T14:04:58-07:00","id":258441,"title":"","content":"What calls to Sidereal fans?<br /> <br /> /is Solar fan","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T14:55:04-07:00","id":258481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercury</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=258440#post258440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I'll tell you what- I'm all for <i>more</i> charms. Of all the complaints I see in this thread, 'I really would like to have a few more Investigation charms' really strikes closest to home.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the increase in the size of the Solar Charmset, I would be <i>shocked</i> if we don't end up deciding to do that with Sidereals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T14:55:44-07:00","id":258482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257997#post257997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't tell if this is praise or criticism...</div> </div> </div> </div>Praise. I'm an English major. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T15:09:53-07:00","id":258489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=258482#post258482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Praise. I'm an English major. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of which, the Sidereal charmset is full of awesome Charm names. Just look at the Socialize Charms; in that one tree alone you find such gems as You and Yours Stance, Wanting and Fearing Prayer, Shun the Smiling Lady, Cash and Murder Games, and Hot-Eyed Snake Whispering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":1120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","user":"Eric Minton","date":". 09-16-2014, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T15:21:38-07:00","id":258500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you clarify how you see it reading that way?</div> </div> </div> </div> I could not quite parse if it meant &quot;it's beautiful and lyrical and highly inventive&quot; or &quot;it's based on the idea of correponding to a bunch of poetry which, while novel, is not the soundest basis for a Charm set&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T15:44:25-07:00","id":258510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ars Fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=258275#post258275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was messed up in the storytellers companion. Everyone immediately saw it was messed up. Folks spent years complaining about how it was messed up and when the Siderial book came out.. the charm was unchanged. How could the developers and writers have missed the years of annoyance that preceded the book? Someone had to copy paste that charm and decide, &quot;No, the guy/gal who wrote the storyteller's companion got this right. It's the people who've actually been playing the game for the past few years who don't get it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Authors don't always check in with fanbases or read forums related to the games they write for. In situations like this, yeah, it's a real shame.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ars Fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=258275#post258275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;No, the guy/gal who wrote the storyteller's companion got this right. It's the people who've actually been playing the game for the past few years who don't get it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Believe it or not, this is a painfully common viewpoint taken at varying times by several different PRG companies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T16:03:13-07:00","id":258515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=258251#post258251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ever since I first read it, I have loved <b>Avoiding the Truth Technique</b>....in theory.<br /> <br /> After I learned a bit more about how social combat and stunting works, however, I realized something: it does literally nothing. You have to stunt your truth-that-is-to-be-seen-as-a-lie to justify using the Charm. But if you just roll a Manipulation check and stunt your social attack as, &quot;I tell him the truth, but in such a way that it sounds preposterous and he thinks I'm either lying or utterly addled, so will dismiss what I'm saying as wholly fictitious,&quot; you get the same effect, but without spending motes and possibly regaining some!<br /> <br /> Avoiding the Truth Technique doesn't even add dice to the roll, not that it would be all that great if it did, because <i>excellencies</i> do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, this is where digging into the history is fun: 1e Avoiding the Truth Technique <i>did</i> add bonus success. It was actually really versatile within the range of &quot;convincing people you were lying,&quot; since it could add to Presence, Socialize, or Bureaucracy (back before social influence had any level of codification).<br /> <br /> Then 2e comes along and gives everyone generic Excellencies. Now Avoiding the Truth Technique just becomes UMI (maybe? the text is unclear) to convince someone you're lying. It also moves to Larceny, for some reason. Of course, 2e Sidereals didn't really take into the account that now we <i>do</i> have rolls for social influence/&quot;attacks,&quot; so it ends up giving this cool concept the mechanical support of a two-legged stool. Glories of the Most High patched this issue generally by giving these Charms specified Willpower costs to resist, which gave Avoiding the Truth some teeth. 2.5 kept the increased Willpower cost, added back in the bonus successes, and also gave it some ability to interfere with truth-detection techniques. For a patch job on top of a patch job, I think it ended up pretty good.<br /> <br /> In 3e, we'll be able to approach Avoiding the Truth Technique free from mechanical baggage, and just do a top-down execution of its really cool concept. I'm optimistic about this going well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T17:31:36-07:00","id":258587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257784#post257784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a concern I share\u2014the 1e Sidereal Charmset was a fucking <i>poem</i>\u2014but have some pretty good ideas of how to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>My feeling was always that it would have been best if 2e had just completely torn down the Sidereal charmset and built a new one in the same spirit, because of how the entire thing unravels if you pull one thread. I sorta feel the same way about 3e, honestly -- it's not possible for a new edition to copy both the letter and the spirit of 1e's Sidereal Charms, and I think the spirit is more important.<br /> <br /> I think if Solars are getting 800 charms Sidereals probably need more, but I <i>am</i> curious to see how you balance that with their traditional thematic of having short, shallow trees that you had to take all or nearly all of in order to reach an apex effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T18:39:14-07:00","id":258605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=258515#post258515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, this is where digging into the history is fun: 1e Avoiding the Truth Technique <i>did</i> add bonus success. It was actually really versatile within the range of &quot;convincing people you were lying,&quot; since it could add to Presence, Socialize, or Bureaucracy (back before social influence had any level of codification).<br /> <br /> Then 2e comes along and gives everyone generic Excellencies. Now Avoiding the Truth Technique just becomes UMI (maybe? the text is unclear) to convince someone you're lying. It also moves to Larceny, for some reason. Of course, 2e Sidereals didn't really take into the account that now we <i>do</i> have rolls for social influence/&quot;attacks,&quot; so it ends up giving this cool concept the mechanical support of a two-legged stool. Glories of the Most High patched this issue generally by giving these Charms specified Willpower costs to resist, which gave Avoiding the Truth some teeth. 2.5 kept the increased Willpower cost, added back in the bonus successes, and also gave it some ability to interfere with truth-detection techniques. For a patch job on top of a patch job, I think it ended up pretty good.<br /> <br /> In 3e, we'll be able to approach Avoiding the Truth Technique free from mechanical baggage, and just do a top-down execution of its really cool concept. I'm optimistic about this going well.</div> </div> </div> </div>SO you gutting the mechanics and keeping the names, and flavor text. I like that approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T19:07:01-07:00","id":258611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257928#post257928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda wonder if anybody here like Unweaving Method, I mean, perfect aggravated attack are nice, and the fluff is awesome too, but since the cost is so high it seem like you can only use the charm two or three times per battle at most.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You mean Iron Siaka ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, you seemed like you were drawing a different person in each panel. Was that on purpose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T20:04:32-07:00","id":258626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=258605#post258605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SO you gutting the mechanics and keeping the names, and flavor text. I like that approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Gutting&quot; makes it sound like we're working with a carcass. What we've got is much better\u2014a clean, blank slate, with a helpful chibi-Past Jenna Moran providing advice and inspiration from the margins. Having nearly burnt my mind out writing the 2.5 errata, I can't emphasize the difference enough!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T21:04:17-07:00","id":258647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=257928#post257928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda wonder if anybody here like Unweaving Method, I mean, perfect aggravated attack are nice, and the fluff is awesome too, but since the cost is so high it seem like you can only use the charm two or three times per battle at most.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did! The flavor was fabulous, and I liked that so much that my 2.0 Chosen of Secrets was actually built to use it as his primary offense in combination with Sidereal Shell Games to boost his damage. He actually filled a pretty valuable niche in combat; our Chosen of Battles had much higher raw numbers, but Kuan could <i>absolutely guarantee</i> that he'd do (Essence x 2) aggravated damage every time he acted unless the enemy used a perfect or had a shaping defense, which was occasionally very valuable when faced with very heavily armored foes. <br /> <br /> Unfortunately the errata basically killed that combo by stripping Shell Games of the ability to affect damage, by making Unweaving Method soakable and by making high armor-based soak much more ubiquitous as a combat strategy. I have an idea of the reasons behind that -- for a combat strategy that involved no combat abilities, it was pretty effective, and Shell Games was admittedly pretty degenerate the way it was -- but I sure do miss it, and I hope 3E keeps Unweaving Method around in a way I won't be abjectly ashamed to use. Because come on, how awesome is it to judge someone's Fate completed, and have Fate itself enforce that judgement by killing them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","name":"ysadrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T21:46:39-07:00","id":258685,"title":"","content":"Weird, I just re-read First Edition Unweaving Method, the fluff is about infecting your enemy with the essence of chaos and ending (since Occult is about understand those stuff and all). But they change that into unraveling the enemy pattern in Second Edition. I wonder what version will the devs chooses for the next Edition.<br /> <br /> Hey, they get rid of &quot;A spirit bird of the Ending House scream whenever someone got hit by Willful Weapon Method and they lose WP&quot; plus &quot;Essence Thorn Practice drag the dead closer to life&quot; from the Thrown charms too. No wonder why people are so angry at Manual: Sidereal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T01:01:34-07:00","id":258849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=258441#post258441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What calls to Sidereal fans?<br /> <br /> /is Solar fan</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally they called to me based on nothing more than what was written up about them in the 1e Core and early books... spirits, prophecy, martial arts mastery, mysteriousness, declaring to fate &quot;thus it shall be&quot;, making hard decisions and beating the impossibly perfect Exalted. I like characters who have uncanny psychic powers to know, who are weak but know where to push at the right time and place.<br /> <br /> So not really, primarily, any of the Sidereals hardback stuff about them having to deal with paperwork, or living in Heaven, or fixing causality errors, or having a lot of limited, finite effects they had to use cleverly and have eureka moments using.<br /> <br /> Not that I hate that stuff, just it's... distinctly... secondary. Very secondary. Not the main taste. I don't really get jazzed up about office politics mixed with Spirited Away, or fixing random purposeless temporal anomalies in the spacetime continuum, or killing random innocents because Destiny Says So. It just feels empty and unsatisfying on its own - Just too much backstage maintenance. It's the ketchup. You don't just eat the ketchup or eat 90% ketchup, 10% food.<br /> <br /> Realistically, that ketchup probably what makes the &quot;play experience&quot; of an all Sidereal group most distinct, and more than a matter of style. Which may be why I like better the idea of Sidereals in a mixed group, with Solars and Lunars and all that, or with Dragonblooded defending the Realm. Away from being Heaven's Task Force and very much in the thick of Creation, salvaging from the ruins of what came before, exploring the vistas mortals live and thrive in and building a new (and if you're an idealist, better) human political order in the world (or upholding the one that's there)., Only using the distinct capabilities of the goddesses of Fate to do so.<br /> <br /> On the other hand (before I get too high on my own supply), Mercury's Sidereal games always sound way fun. So there's that. With a good enough presentation and sales pitch...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T03:11:14-07:00","id":258891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cenobite451</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=258425#post258425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really hope the closed Charmset primarily filled with weird gimmicky stuff remains a thing. I mean, it'd be nice for it to be <i>useful</i> weird gimmicky stuff, but honestly if it came down to one or the other I'd personally choose to keep the &quot;saving the world with some pocket lint, three feet of twine and a spork&quot; thing over having a well-rounded Charmset with nary a second thought.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*braces for imminent stabbing*</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm OK as long as the charms allow you to ACTUALLY save the world like that.<br /> <br /> If they come up just as &quot;your best shot at saving the world would be with some pocket lint, three feet of twine and a spork. But you WILL fail because the charms are broken, or there are gaping holes in your skill set&quot; then NO<br /> <br /> The maidens may be weird, but they are (or should) also be very good at analysis, prediction and foreseeing the future, especially having access to samsara. Designing a hugely flawed charmset that shoots in the feet of their chose, unless for an explicitly justified reason, in NOT what they would do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T05:08:32-07:00","id":258928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack In The Box</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=258891#post258891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they come up just as &quot;your best shot at saving the world would be with some pocket lint, three feet of twine and a spork. But you WILL fail because the charms are broken, or there are gaping holes in your skill set&quot; then NO</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you legitimately concerned that the devs will implement something like this?<br /> <br /> Also, nobody's Charms include Save the World Technique. Even if Solars are the only ones capable of curing a person of the Great Contagion with their native Charmset, it would have taken a hell of a lot more than Ailment-Rectifying Method to stop 90% of Creation's population from dying.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T05:29:00-07:00","id":258933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=258928#post258928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you legitimately concerned that the devs will implement something like this?<br /> <br /> Also, nobody's Charms include Save the World Technique. Even if Solars are the only ones capable of curing a person of the Great Contagion with their native Charmset, it would have taken a hell of a lot more than Ailment-Rectifying Method to stop 90% of Creation's population from dying.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was just aswering to someone basically saying &quot;I like the weird style of sidereals more than their mechanical efficiency&quot;, by saying &quot;yes up to a point. Having stylish powers is meaningless if you are doomed to fail against any other splat that actually has mechanically well-designed trees&quot;.<br /> <br /> The actual point had nothing to do with what the current devs are plaining and my confidence in them, nor with saving the world specifically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T06:38:30-07:00","id":258942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack In The Box</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=258933#post258933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The actual point had nothing to do with... saving the world specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you mentioned it with that exact wording no less than twice for no specific reason?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T06:46:28-07:00","id":258944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=258942#post258942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you mentioned it with that exact wording no less than twice for no specific reason?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe because Cenobite used that exact wording to talk about the flavor of the Sidereal Charm set?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T09:38:27-07:00","id":259018,"title":"","content":"Hey look, knives! Good thing I'm properly braced. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/471-cenobite451","name":"Cenobite451","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar471_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T10:19:46-07:00","id":259029,"title":"","content":"I kinda wish that Chosen of Journey's anima power is more useful, I mean, increase movement speed fit with them being Mercury's chosen and all, but it's just so, i don't know, niche ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T11:32:55-07:00","id":259070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=259029#post259029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda wish that Chosen of Journey's anima power is more useful, I mean, increase movement speed fit with them being Mercury's chosen and all, but it's just so, i don't know, niche ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah practically it doesn't come up that much since Exalted does not try to be a minis game with super-strict range and movement increments, or at the very least those stop mattering when Charms are involved. It's certainly a super-weak anima compared to, oh, the Serenity power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T14:28:51-07:00","id":259240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=258441#post258441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What calls to Sidereal fans?<br /> <br /> /is Solar fan</div> </div> </div> </div>I was mostly a DB fan for 2e because I didn't like the direction most solar charms pushed the story, but Sids were probably my second favourite. I liked two things about them. One was how their charms were generally powerful at what they did, but funky in their implementation. At least I thought they were powerful at the time. Shun the Smiling Lady, Neighbourhood Relocation Scheme, ect. You could move a whole city! Even Solars would have trouble doing that efficiently. But what good was it? Well that's what you had to figure out, how to apply it.<br /> <br /> The other thing was their background fluff infrastructure stuff. When the gods fail and Creation really needs some help, the Sidereals come in. Able to deploy anywhere in creation like ninja shock troops. I liked the idea of having a team of five stargating all over the world simultaneously being ninja assassins and Big Damn Heroes. They weren't warlords or kings high priests, they did a thankless job but apart from factional infighting on key issues they were pretty much on the same side, and that side was usually not a bad one.<br /> <br /> Also the Sidereals in the opening comic were the only signature circle that seemed to like each other, have fun and genuinely represent a good PC group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T14:30:30-07:00","id":259242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=259070#post259070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah practically it doesn't come up that much since Exalted does not try to be a minis game with super-strict range and movement increments, or at the very least those stop mattering when Charms are involved. It's certainly a super-weak anima compared to, oh, the Serenity power.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may change in the next edition, one of the spoilers had a movement pool of dice for escaping/catching a fleeing opponent. It might be a lot more important now to have a big movement dice pool. Unless things have changed in the past few months anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T14:53:10-07:00","id":259267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=258441#post258441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What calls to Sidereal fans?<br /> <br /> /is Solar fan</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I apologize that this response took so long- I was busy elsewhere for a while.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'd ascribe it to a few factors:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Agency</b> - specifically that a Sidereal is, by default, an agent of order. Heaven in the specific sense, sure, but even if you wipe out Yu-Shan you can still fit them as agents of fate or destiny as you'd like. Among my favorite set of short stories are the <i>Traveler in Black</i> sets, which is an archetypal inspiration for the splat, When I was a student of Christian mythology, my favorite stories were always the ones featuring the angels rather than the ones with more direct interaction with God. There's something very <i>satisfying</i> about service to a higher agency.*<br /> <br /> <b>2. Reality-Bending Magic</b> - one could say that all magic bends reality, I suppose. People have noted before that Sidereal magic is less about who you are and more like a set of special sorceries; I quite like that, at least to a point. You really feel like you've been given a set of cheat codes, or perhaps access to console commands (but you only know so many commands!). I've seen people build entire characters around having Avoidance Kata, and I've built characters entirely around both Mirror-Shattering Method and Godly Familiar.** There's a sense of significance which Jenna Moran tried to imbue the Sidereal charms with, and I personally think she succeeded to some extent.<br /> <br /> <b>3. I'm a Massive Asshole</b> - If I could be that guy in shows who appears and knows everything and vanishes if you try to grab him, I would do it. Fuck, that sounds like fun. Anyway, even if you don't actually know everything, there's nobody like a Sidereal for looking like an omniscient dickbag.<br /> <br /> <b>4. Spirit Moderation</b> - There's way too much redundancy in 2e, but I always loved the idea of being a moderator between the spirits and the world. Or, since the Immaculates mostly have that covered these days, the spirits and Heaven. Second role gives me way more opportunity to threaten spirits anywho.<br /> <br /> <b>5. Philosophy</b> - the Exalted aren't tied to philosophies by any means. The Solars don't have to be virtue ethicists, the Alchemicals don't have to like socialism and the Lunars are thankfully free forever of mandatory worship of pulp-barbarianism. Yet there are connotations in the gameline, and the Sidereals are the obvious consequentialists. We all know which side of the Trolley Problem Chejop Kejak finds himself on. I have great sympathy for their anti-heroic image of the Men Who Did A Terrible Deed Because The Ends Do Justify The Means, even if there's a very real question about exactly how justified they were.<br /> <br /> <b>6. Story</b> - as I hinted in the first paragraph, I like playing as the agent of a higher power. While you can certainly finagle that as a Solar or Lunar player, the background's set up differently and I think the game tends to push people in other ways. Solars are the returning god-kings, come back to save the world! Only I have an aesthetic dislike for 'returning god-kings' and I don't really feel qualified to save the world. I prefer to moderate the attempts of others to do so! Abyssals are the vengeful champions of the dead, destined to end all Creation! But I don't want to end Creation and I don't like Abyssal thematics! Infernals are the last hurrah of the scheming Primordials, who may return Creation to the days before days or spur it to new and undreampt-of heights! Meh.***<br /> <br /> But Sidereals are the overworked, harried overseers of Creation since the dawn of Ages. They've achieved jurisdiction over all things and everything is slipping through their fingers! They are bound by strange laws, but wield power which the world does not even suspect exists! They're the servants of gods and the masters of gods! They work with supreme dedication even when all their hopes have perished! I like all of that. I like it a lot.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *As someone who has worked for several different government bureaus, I really like how Exalted took inspiration from the Chinese conceptualization of Heaven and melded the numinous with the mundane. It echoes the feeling I've had while working for agencies which have goals I respect and yet require a certain amount of soul-crushing work and banal office politicking. It's a beautiful mixture of determined pride and weary cynicism. <br /> <br /> **I had an idea for an Oracle-hacker in space-Shards who would be built around using Willing Assumption of Chains to hijack gods, but I never got to try that and I think it would have needed a very careful ST to moderate.<br /> <br /> ***I don't know what the shit Lunars are supposed to do, so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T15:45:34-07:00","id":259315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack In The Box</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=258891#post258891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they come up just as &quot;your best shot at saving the world would be with some pocket lint, three feet of twine and a spork. But you WILL fail because the charms are broken, or there are gaping holes in your skill set&quot; then NO</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed! However, Sids really only had this problem in 2e, and then only because 2e's Sidereal charmset was a hatchet job. There's no real reason to think that a Sidereal charmset designed with care would look like this, since it's never happened in the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T20:15:49-07:00","id":259457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=258441#post258441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What calls to Sidereal fans?<br /> <br /> /is Solar fan</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, pretty much what Mercury and the Love Monkey said. (As an aside, I would totally watch a show called Mercury and the Love Monkey.) Also, I like MacGyver - but he'd be <i>hugely</i> less entertaining if he ever had exactly the right tools for the job.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, Siddies aren't my <i>favorite</i> splat; that spot's reserved for Abyssals (who also sometimes have the MacGyver thing going for/against them when they're trying to be the heroes). But the Chosen of the Maidens run a close second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/471-cenobite451","name":"Cenobite451","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar471_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T08:32:48-07:00","id":259784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=258441#post258441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What calls to Sidereal fans?<br /> <br /> /is Solar fan</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I took some time to be sure to express clearly my thoughts about it, and in the mean time mercury already said much about what I wanted.<br /> <br /> I'll just add that, a few exemple charms to that I consider, in their design, essential to the sidereal style :<br /> <br /> - narrow and strong, like someone else's destiny. A charm that works only for poisons (+diseases and crippling effects in 2.5 IIRC) which are not really common except in specific campaigns, but allows for totally reverse some situations unlike any other poison-resisting charm (there isn't even a resistance roll I think). <br /> <br /> - &quot;weak&quot; charms (meaning charms that don't do extremely potent effects) that comboes well with others or opens interesting stunts, like presence in absence technique or sidereal shell-games.<br /> <br /> <br /> I like the sidereal style to be like &quot;playing&quot; a game of pachinko (i guess that's how it's called) :<br /> the events are like a ball, and you want it to fall in one of the desired outcomes<br /> first, you use wide but weak charms to influence the events slightly untill they fit the situation where your narrow but strong charms give you a strong impact.<br /> <br /> Just like if you want to make a king change his mind on a decision, you can use and abuse presence in abscence technique and avoiding the truth technique until he no longer trusts the gounds on which he based his decision, then you can introduce another option and seal the deal with force decision.<br /> <br /> That's the &quot;trinity&quot; of sidereal gameplay for me, opposed to solar's straightforward charms : influence the events by small bits like a buterfly effect and then with one or 2 powerful but situational charms reap the effects.<br /> <br /> As a side note, this style sure works well with plaing, but it could also work well with improvising plans. I say that because I don't think sids should always be weaker in combat (for instance) if they didn't plan it ahead. Instead I find they should be weaker only if they fail to adapt and improvise a plan to the situation. That's why i'm not as attached to avoidance kata as other players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T09:17:32-07:00","id":259796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cenobite451</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=259457#post259457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, pretty much what Mercury and the Love Monkey said. (As an aside, I would totally watch a show called Mercury and the Love Monkey.) Also, I like MacGyver - but he'd be <i>hugely</i> less entertaining if he ever had exactly the right tools for the job.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, Siddies aren't my <i>favorite</i> splat; that spot's reserved for Abyssals (who also sometimes have the MacGyver thing going for/against them when they're trying to be the heroes). But the Chosen of the Maidens run a close second.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about &quot;Sidereals as MacGyver&quot; or &quot;Sidereals as Bond/Maidens as Q&quot; is this: MacGyver never has exactly the right tools for the job, but he also always has exactly the right combination of random objects to do what he needs to do the job. Similarly, every gadget Bond receives from Q, no matter how bizarre, will always be used at some point before the end of the film.<br /> <br /> The difference is that unlike MacGyver, and unlike Bond, the guys writing the Charmset are not the same guys writing the script. Sidereal Charms can be weird and wacky, but they also have to actually cover all of the things that they need in order to do their job in a generally applicable manner, and I would say that in cases where these functions collide the latter should win out over the former.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T09:46:51-07:00","id":259814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=259796#post259796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about &quot;Sidereals as MacGyver&quot; or &quot;Sidereals as Bond/Maidens as Q&quot; is this: MacGyver never has exactly the right tools for the job, but he also always has exactly the right combination of random objects to do what he needs to do the job. Similarly, every gadget Bond receives from Q, no matter how bizarre, will always be used at some point before the end of the film.<br /> <br /> The difference is that unlike MacGyver, and unlike Bond, the guys writing the Charmset are not the same guys writing the script.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but only to a degree. MacGyver's challenge is <i>picking</i> the right combination of random objects to do the job, even though individually it generally seems as though they really shouldn't. The way the Charmset facilitates this sort of thing is largely by giving us a big toolbox full of Awesome-but-(often <i>wildly</i>)-Impractical random shit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=259796#post259796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereal Charms can be weird and wacky, but they also have to actually cover all of the things that they need in order to do their job in a generally applicable manner, and I would say that in cases where these functions collide the latter should win out over the former.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess all I can really say is that I disagree. &quot;Generally applicable&quot; is the sticking point really; a version of the Sidereals that <i>doesn't</i> force the Sids (and by extension their players) to employ a degree of lateral thinking to solve their problems is a version that completely loses my interest.<br /> <br /> Also, one must remember that even if they somehow find themselves without a single Charm applicable to the situation, a Sidereal's still no less capable than a heroic mortal, and this is supposedly the edition to finally terminate the tradition of mortals-can't-do-shit. At the end of the day, you can get a whole lot of general utility out of just, y'know, <i>being human</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">...also also, apparently italics are my new semicolons.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":471,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/471-cenobite451","user":"Cenobite451","date":". 09-18-2014, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/471-cenobite451","name":"Cenobite451","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar471_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T12:46:54-07:00","id":259967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cenobite451</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=259814#post259814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess all I can really say is that I disagree. &quot;Generally applicable&quot; is the sticking point really; a version of the Sidereals that <i>doesn't</i> force the Sids (and by extension their players) to employ a degree of lateral thinking to solve their problems is a version that completely loses my interest.[/SIZE]</div> </div> </div> </div>But does every single Charm need to require weird lateral thinking to facilitate application? Some of that is cool but after a time I can't see that requirement for all Charms as being anything other than exhausting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T14:13:04-07:00","id":260073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=259967#post259967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But does every single Charm need to require weird lateral thinking to facilitate application? Some of that is cool but after a time I can't see that requirement for all Charms as being anything other than exhausting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what you're worried about is nothing more than a bit of meme expansion.<br /> <br /> If we ignore 2e Sidereals, as is right and proper, 1e's structure should give us some idea of how the devs will approach 3e. In 1e, Sidereals had short trees with very deliberate holes, but they didn't exactly have 'a rubber band, a toothpick and a zippo' or anything like that. Sidereal charms were enormously powerful. The 'McGuyver' aspect, such as it existed, came from manipulating the situation such that one of your ridiculous charms was applicable to it. Lateral thinking was an element, but not something which was unduly burdensome nor universal.*<br /> <br /> The archetypal example from 1e was always Avoiding the Truth Technique. 'Sidereals don't have the ability to make someone believe that what they're saying is the truth!', a commentator would announce, 'You've got to make them believe that you're lying in a way which accomplishes your goal!' I'm here to tell you today that this is and has always been <i>really easy.</i> A simple inversion often accomplishes it! Look:<br /> <br /> <b>Solar</b> &quot;Know that my words are truth! The Immaculate order is evil and the Solars are magnificent god-kings!&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Pitiful Mortal</b> &quot;Right-o!&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Sidereal</b> &quot;You've heard of the Cult of the Illuminated? Murderers and thieves! The Solars are not magnificent, nor are they god-kings! The Immaculate Order is truth and light!&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Pitiful Mortal</b> &quot;Theoretically I could believe that you are lying and yet still incidentally correct. In practice, however, my powerful belief that you're telling lies inclines me strongly toward a positive belief in the converse. Still, as I am a worthy philosopher-peasant, I shall carefully weigh the possibilities and make a concerted cho-&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Sidereal</b> &quot;Force Decision, you believe the opposite of what I said!&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Philosopher Pitiful Mortal </b>&quot;Oh, balls.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's another thing, of course. Sidereals get charms like Force Decision, or Unweaving Method, or Duck Fate- powerful, straightforward and with wide applicability. There's a reason that a number of people in 1e thought that Sidereals were far too powerful.<br /> <br /> Not that I condone such blasphemies, you understand.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *I mean, sure, There's some lateral thinking involved in making Neighborhood Relocation Scheme solve a problem, but I've never seen anyone get frustrated and shout 'How am I supposed to work with only the power to re-shape the face of Creation at my will?!'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T14:37:55-07:00","id":260084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *I mean, sure, There's some lateral thinking involved in making Neighborhood Relocation Scheme solve a problem, but I've never seen anyone get frustrated and shout 'How am I supposed to work with only the power to re-shape the face of Creation at my will?!' </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, it cannot save Gem from exploding because the volcano and fire dust mines are part of the city<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T14:49:32-07:00","id":260100,"title":"","content":"An E10 Solar could invent Glorious Golden Save Gem From Exploding Prana and it wouldn't be able to save Gem from exploding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T14:53:41-07:00","id":260104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack In The Box</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=259784#post259784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the sidereal style to be like &quot;playing&quot; a game of pachinko (i guess that's how it's called) :<br /> the events are like a ball, and you want it to fall in one of the desired outcomes<br /> first, you use wide but weak charms to influence the events slightly untill they fit the situation where your narrow but strong charms give you a strong impact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this image - Sidereals generally feeling like they have a lot of effects that feel &quot;weak&quot; but allow them to flexibly and dextrously manipulate events until they are at the point where they can push hard (or hard enough) to make a change feels right, while Solars would seem like they should have more effects that just feel exultingly, brazenly and brashly strong.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Writing a set of Charms which look inadequate to do the job without actually being inadequate to do the job seems very challenging. <br /> <br /> Seems much harder than writing a bunch of Charms which both are adequate to do the job, and look adequate, and can be added to at any time if they're not.<br /> <br /> I don't know how the writers could be sure they'd got it quite right. A lot of it would just having to be putting stuff out there and hoping for the best? To some extent if they did, as soon as they'd explained to us how the set was actually adequate for the job, they'd sort of collapse the illusion. (Don't worry, I'm not going to talk about Schrodinger's Charmset in a non-physicist who will mangle it horribly sort of way at this juncture).<br /> <br /> You definitely need a lot of GM and group commitment to finessing play and interpreting Charms broadly to make it work. <br /> <br /> I think I agree with Couch here that what the GM and group should certainly not have to do is redefine the problems the Sids have to face and the great deeds they should be able to do from what the books say they are, to problems and great deeds which may not be what the books give as their goals, but which they can actually solve through lateral thinking and their Charmset, and then call it good (taking the terminal meme expansion view that the all important thing is the lateral thinking... leave aside whether they're actually succeeding at the sort of great deeds Sidereals should do).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T17:26:43-07:00","id":260196,"title":"","content":"When you had an obvious problem that you couldn't finagle with, or needed to approach something head-on and all your native tools are circuitous, the traditional way for a Sidereal to handle it is by application of a Martial Art, probably one of the weirder ones that feels less like an &quot;I fite u&quot; style and more of the &quot;other Ability crossover&quot; stuff like Ebon Shadow or SVN, to say nothing of the weirdness possible in SMA.<br /> <br /> While I understand that's part of their designed play experience, I just wonder if that paradigm is <i>desirable</i>. It seems to take some of the &quot;cleverness&quot; out of the Sidereal Charmset when the &quot;easiest&quot; solution to a problem is just using Martial Arts. You set up a situation where you cannot deal with a problem in the same way as other Exalts because your Charms don't work that way, then give the loophole that with the right MA, <i>you totally can deal with a problem the same way</i>.<br /> <br /> Perhaps this will no longer be the case in 3e, but there are going to be a number of the more esoteric non-SMA Styles released as early as the Core (SVN, Ebon Shadow, Black Claw, and Crane come to mind). So, I just wonder if the old paradigm is desirable because it basically undercuts itself and the exception swallows the rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T19:47:21-07:00","id":260282,"title":"","content":"My impression was that the <i>traditional</i> way to approach it was to just use the abilities and capacities you actually had, assuming we're talking about 1e here. Almost all the 1e Sidereal players I've heard tales of had stories about how they figured out a clever way to solve a problem that their toolset seemed really ill-suited for using just what they had on hand, whereas I've never heard of any who learned MA to solve a specific problem that wasn't &quot;I want a different perfect/persistent defense&quot;. Many learned MA because it was <i>awesome</i>, but that's a bit distinct. Keep in mind that in the ess 1-3 area, the Sidereal non-MA combat abilities were pretty great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T22:42:20-07:00","id":260374,"title":"","content":"Soooooo......about Sidereal Thrown, I wonder if Unrelenting Torment Technique will have its damage be unsoakble again like in First Edition. Also, should Essence Thorn Practice be kick off from the tree so a weapon-using Sidereal can reach the capstone without having to worry about learning a mediocre Spirit-Weapon charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T22:59:39-07:00","id":260381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=260374#post260374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soooooo......about Sidereal Thrown, I wonder if Unrelenting Torment Technique will have its damage be unsoakble again like in First Edition. Also, should Essence Thorn Practice be kick off from the tree so a weapon-using Sidereal can reach the capstone without having to worry about learning a mediocre Spirit-Weapon charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or they could make that charm worth buying? Or just get rid of it entirely because they are rebuilding from the ground up so nothing is assured to return.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T23:29:46-07:00","id":260389,"title":"","content":"<b>Ghosthead: </b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=258849#post258849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally they called to me based on nothing more than what was written up about them in the 1e Core and early books... spirits, prophecy, martial arts mastery, mysteriousness, declaring to fate &quot;thus it shall be&quot;, making hard decisions and beating the impossibly perfect Exalted. I like characters who have uncanny psychic powers to know, who are weak but know where to push at the right time and place.<br /> <br /> So not really, primarily, any of the Sidereals hardback stuff about them having to deal with paperwork, or living in Heaven, or fixing causality errors, or having a lot of limited, finite effects they had to use cleverly and have eureka moments using.<br /> <br /> Not that I hate that stuff, just it's... distinctly... secondary. Very secondary. Not the main taste. I don't really get jazzed up about office politics mixed with Spirited Away, or fixing random purposeless temporal anomalies in the spacetime continuum, or killing random innocents because Destiny Says So. It just feels empty and unsatisfying on its own - Just too much backstage maintenance. It's the ketchup. You don't just eat the ketchup or eat 90% ketchup, 10% food.<br /> <br /> Realistically, that ketchup probably what makes the &quot;play experience&quot; of an all Sidereal group most distinct, and more than a matter of style. Which may be why I like better the idea of Sidereals in a mixed group, with Solars and Lunars and all that, or with Dragonblooded defending the Realm. Away from being Heaven's Task Force and very much in the thick of Creation, salvaging from the ruins of what came before, exploring the vistas mortals live and thrive in and building a new (and if you're an idealist, better) human political order in the world (or upholding the one that's there)., Only using the distinct capabilities of the goddesses of Fate to do so.<br /> <br /> On the other hand (before I get too high on my own supply), Mercury's Sidereal games always sound way fun. So there's that. With a good enough presentation and sales pitch...</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Mercury: </b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercury</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=259267#post259267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I apologize that this response took so long- I was busy elsewhere for a while.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'd ascribe it to a few factors:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Agency</b> - specifically that a Sidereal is, by default, an agent of order. Heaven in the specific sense, sure, but even if you wipe out Yu-Shan you can still fit them as agents of fate or destiny as you'd like. Among my favorite set of short stories are the <i>Traveler in Black</i> sets, which is an archetypal inspiration for the splat, When I was a student of Christian mythology, my favorite stories were always the ones featuring the angels rather than the ones with more direct interaction with God. There's something very <i>satisfying</i> about service to a higher agency.*<br /> <br /> <b>2. Reality-Bending Magic</b> - one could say that all magic bends reality, I suppose. People have noted before that Sidereal magic is less about who you are and more like a set of special sorceries; I quite like that, at least to a point. You really feel like you've been given a set of cheat codes, or perhaps access to console commands (but you only know so many commands!). I've seen people build entire characters around having Avoidance Kata, and I've built characters entirely around both Mirror-Shattering Method and Godly Familiar.** There's a sense of significance which Jenna Moran tried to imbue the Sidereal charms with, and I personally think she succeeded to some extent.<br /> <br /> <b>3. I'm a Massive Asshole</b> - If I could be that guy in shows who appears and knows everything and vanishes if you try to grab him, I would do it. Fuck, that sounds like fun. Anyway, even if you don't actually know everything, there's nobody like a Sidereal for looking like an omniscient dickbag.<br /> <br /> <b>4. Spirit Moderation</b> - There's way too much redundancy in 2e, but I always loved the idea of being a moderator between the spirits and the world. Or, since the Immaculates mostly have that covered these days, the spirits and Heaven. Second role gives me way more opportunity to threaten spirits anywho.<br /> <br /> <b>5. Philosophy</b> - the Exalted aren't tied to philosophies by any means. The Solars don't have to be virtue ethicists, the Alchemicals don't have to like socialism and the Lunars are thankfully free forever of mandatory worship of pulp-barbarianism. Yet there are connotations in the gameline, and the Sidereals are the obvious consequentialists. We all know which side of the Trolley Problem Chejop Kejak finds himself on. I have great sympathy for their anti-heroic image of the Men Who Did A Terrible Deed Because The Ends Do Justify The Means, even if there's a very real question about exactly how justified they were.<br /> <br /> <b>6. Story</b> - as I hinted in the first paragraph, I like playing as the agent of a higher power. While you can certainly finagle that as a Solar or Lunar player, the background's set up differently and I think the game tends to push people in other ways. Solars are the returning god-kings, come back to save the world! Only I have an aesthetic dislike for 'returning god-kings' and I don't really feel qualified to save the world. I prefer to moderate the attempts of others to do so! Abyssals are the vengeful champions of the dead, destined to end all Creation! But I don't want to end Creation and I don't like Abyssal thematics! Infernals are the last hurrah of the scheming Primordials, who may return Creation to the days before days or spur it to new and undreampt-of heights! Meh.***<br /> <br /> But Sidereals are the overworked, harried overseers of Creation since the dawn of Ages. They've achieved jurisdiction over all things and everything is slipping through their fingers! They are bound by strange laws, but wield power which the world does not even suspect exists! They're the servants of gods and the masters of gods! They work with supreme dedication even when all their hopes have perished! I like all of that. I like it a lot.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *As someone who has worked for several different government bureaus, I really like how Exalted took inspiration from the Chinese conceptualization of Heaven and melded the numinous with the mundane. It echoes the feeling I've had while working for agencies which have goals I respect and yet require a certain amount of soul-crushing work and banal office politicking. It's a beautiful mixture of determined pride and weary cynicism.<br /> <br /> **I had an idea for an Oracle-hacker in space-Shards who would be built around using Willing Assumption of Chains to hijack gods, but I never got to try that and I think it would have needed a very careful ST to moderate.<br /> <br /> ***I don't know what the shit Lunars are supposed to do, so.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Love Monkey</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=259240#post259240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was mostly a DB fan for 2e because I didn't like the direction most solar charms pushed the story, but Sids were probably my second favourite. I liked two things about them. One was how their charms were generally powerful at what they did, but funky in their implementation. At least I thought they were powerful at the time. Shun the Smiling Lady, Neighbourhood Relocation Scheme, ect. You could move a whole city! Even Solars would have trouble doing that efficiently. But what good was it? Well that's what you had to figure out, how to apply it.<br /> <br /> The other thing was their background fluff infrastructure stuff. When the gods fail and Creation really needs some help, the Sidereals come in. Able to deploy anywhere in creation like ninja shock troops. I liked the idea of having a team of five stargating all over the world simultaneously being ninja assassins and Big Damn Heroes. They weren't warlords or kings high priests, they did a thankless job but apart from factional infighting on key issues they were pretty much on the same side, and that side was usually not a bad one.<br /> <br /> Also the Sidereals in the opening comic were the only signature circle that seemed to like each other, have fun and genuinely represent a good PC group.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Oooh, this is all very interesting.<br /> <br /> Thank you for sharing that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T01:54:40-07:00","id":260444,"title":"","content":"I'm mostly going by the Sidereal game I'm in, so I don't know how this relates to other people's experiences.<br /> But being an agent of fate readily allows you to move from a high stakes mission to stop a demon doing untold amounts of damage to something low key like ensuring two people fall in love like they're supposed to.<br /> With my Solars, after dealing with something on the scale of the former often made involving myself in mortal affairs feel a bit like kicking over an ant hill.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T02:45:01-07:00","id":260458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=260374#post260374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soooooo......about Sidereal Thrown, I wonder if Unrelenting Torment Technique will have its damage be unsoakble again like in First Edition. Also, should Essence Thorn Practice be kick off from the tree so a weapon-using Sidereal can reach the capstone without having to worry about learning a mediocre Spirit-Weapon charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're worrying wayyyyyyy too much about very specific mechanics at this juncture, when the baseline game engine itself has yet to be officially released. Comparisons to 1e Charm <i>themes</i> might be appropriate but comparisons to 1e Charm <i>mechanics</i> are another thing entirely, let alone the concrete details of Charm tree structure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=260444#post260444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm mostly going by the Sidereal game I'm in, so I don't know how this relates to other people's experiences.<br /> But being an agent of fate readily allows you to move from a high stakes mission to stop a demon doing untold amounts of damage to something low key like ensuring two people fall in love like they're supposed to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope this doesn't come across the wrong way but do people find playing situations like this......fun?<br /> <br /> I guess to me it would be like taking on a project management role for a big new task at work and then after doing it really well, spending two weeks doing nothing but making copies. I guess I'd find it hard not to think of a Sidereal doing a great job on the former just feeling really bitter if their next task was dealing with mortal stuff, unless said mortal stuff was itself pretty complicated and equally important. I'd think even a lot of Sidereals would sigh and roll their eyes if this was considered normal workflow treatment.<br /> <br /> I dunno, I'd consider &quot;great job stamping out that Yozi cult, no go make sure these two kiss at the right time&quot; to be kind of asymmetrically weird as contiguous plot arcs, unless the latter involved undermining some supernatural political or malevolent influence trying to prevent said kiss because Reasons and exerting Essence and resources to preventing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 09-19-2014, 05:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T03:00:57-07:00","id":260464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=260458#post260458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, I'd consider &quot;great job stamping out that Yozi cult, no go make sure these two kiss at the right time&quot; to be kind of asymmetrically weird as contiguous plot arcs, unless the latter involved undermining some supernatural political or malevolent influence trying to prevent said kiss because Reasons and exerting Essence and resources to preventing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd think it was more &quot;make sure a suitably appealing (if not actually epic) romance occurs&quot;. It's not about the basic timing, but the overall narrative weave.<br /> <br /> It might be a bit like being Death of the Discworld or the Endless; you're part of the overall cosmological constant, but you've also got to get in there and engage with certain events personally every now and then, because that's basically what you get from anthropomorphizing major universal abstractions.<br /> <br /> Sidereal Exalted aren't personifications, but they're working in a fairly similar position.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, it might be an occasion of furthering particular plans they have for some time down the road. Like a kind of reversal of Back to the Future, and where Marty McFly will do something important in a manner that makes ensuring his existence matter to anybody besides himself.<br /> <br /> Either way, a sense of esoteric importance to the little things in the world, that would appear to me as implicit in the concept and setting space that Sidereals occupy, and part of the appeal therein. One just has to avoid a presentation of it being a trivial or perfunctory task.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T03:34:13-07:00","id":260486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=258441#post258441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What calls to Sidereal fans?<br /> <br /> /is Solar fan</div> </div> </div> </div>To me at least, a big part of it is the being part of something greater than yourself, being an agent enacting more than your whims. Solars work from a very self-focused position - they are all about their own ideals, though sometimes they might have one of these ideals be the following of some other person. They are classic western heroes, beholden to nothing but either themselves or their own loyalty to their beloved lord. Sidereals, on the other hand, start out with a baseline assumption of being <i>agents </i>for cosmic forces and committees that deliberate how to make the world keep turning. Where Solars are Kings and Heroes, free to go around and happen to everyone else, Sidereals have a <i>job </i>to do, and are given enough knowledge and perspective to understand how horribly important this job is. They are Men in Black, toiling away unknown in the shadows, so that there is still a sunrise tomorrow while the Solars in the daylight shake the realms and change the lives of men.<br /> <br /> Basically, all Exalts can come to bear the shackles of understanding the fragility of the forces that keep Creation as we know it working - but only for Sidereals are these shackles quite literally part of the introductory package and come with a specific job to keep it going. This creates a certain agent of heaven/MIB/SWAT role and narrative that I rather enjoy over the kingdom building of other splats.<br /> <br /> It's related to why I enjoy Alchemicals so much as well.<br /> <br /> And there is also the more... low-height feel of them. It's hard to explain, but a lot of Exalted feels like you are <i>supposed </i>to be visibly above things, being always a big player and such and if you aren't you're doing it wrong, while with sidereals it feels like you're encouraged to solve your problems with the absolute minimum of fuss - a perfect Sidereal is the one who, like Lu-Tze, can change the course of history by breaking off one lever with nobody even knowing or helping a single man come to an epiphany. They feel like they are more encouraged to get a bit more involved in the details. And I like going down to the details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1793,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","user":"Drascin","date":". 09-19-2014, 06:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T04:06:10-07:00","id":260495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=260458#post260458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">some supernatural political or malevolent influence trying to prevent said kiss because Reasons and exerting Essence and resources to preventing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although now I've got this image of a tendency among the Fair Folk going around trying to induce argumentative rom-com bullshit because they think it makes for a more interesting experience of people falling in love, and many Chosen of Serenity working to make it... not that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T05:15:12-07:00","id":260530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=260464#post260464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd think it was more &quot;make sure a suitably appealing (if not actually epic) romance occurs&quot;. It's not about the basic timing, but the overall narrative weave.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. A lot of our dealings with mortal level problems are a reminder that great things can have small beginnings.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T05:19:56-07:00","id":260533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=260495#post260495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although now I've got this image of a tendency among the Fair Folk going around trying to induce argumentative rom-com bullshit because they think it makes for a more interesting experience of people falling in love, and many Chosen of Serenity working to make it... not that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, Venus has some very interesting views on what love is.<br /> <br /> My kind of &quot;ideal&quot; Sidereal &quot;mundane&quot; mission is kinda like Romeo &amp; Juliet. Except both sides in the Montague/Capulet feud have different supernatural backers trying to win that family's superiority and both sides will go to any length to sabotage peace, and a &quot;Sidereal victory&quot; is creating a happy engagement that resolves the blood feud. Which probably involves neutralizing the supernatural backers more than anything else.<br /> <br /> And on the other end of that, End Debate/Force Decision worry me a little in terms of story trivializing, though this is more of a 2e perspective. I think the 3e Intimacy mechanics should make it such that a Sidereal using Force Decision doesn't casually get to overwrite the Defining Intimacy of Capulet hating the Montagues, because 3e Charm theory and so on and so forth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T05:41:20-07:00","id":260537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=260486#post260486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where Solars are Kings and Heroes, free to go around and happen to everyone else, Sidereals have a <i>job </i>to do, and are given enough knowledge and perspective to understand how horribly important this job is. They are Men in Black, toiling away unknown in the shadows, so that there is still a sunrise tomorrow while the Solars in the daylight shake the realms and change the lives of men.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;There's always an Arquillian Battle Cruiser, or a Corillian Death Ray, or an intergalactic plague that is about to wipe out all life on this miserable little planet, and the only way these people can get on with their happy lives is that they Do. Not. Know about it!&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/471-cenobite451","name":"Cenobite451","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar471_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T06:17:28-07:00","id":260568,"title":"","content":"Why does people always insist that the Lover is the only constellation of the House of Serenity anyway. The other four constellations pretty much are all about happiness, friendship and joy in living and yet people always latch onto the Lover as the thing that represent the Maiden's view on love. Just because the Sidereal said it doesn't make it true.<br /> <br /> To be honest though, I do think that Venus (and her sister) IS a sicko :'P She probably happy that a person getting married/raped just happen according to Fate schedule.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T08:07:37-07:00","id":260604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=259796#post259796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about &quot;Sidereals as MacGyver&quot; or &quot;Sidereals as Bond/Maidens as Q&quot; is this: MacGyver never has exactly the right tools for the job, but he also always has exactly the right combination of random objects to do what he needs to do the job. Similarly, every gadget Bond receives from Q, no matter how bizarre, will always be used at some point before the end of the film.<br /> <br /> The difference is that unlike MacGyver, and unlike Bond, the guys writing the Charmset are not the same guys writing the script. Sidereal Charms can be weird and wacky, but they also have to actually cover all of the things that they need in order to do their job in a generally applicable manner, and I would say that in cases where these functions collide the latter should win out over the former.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cenobite451</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=259814#post259814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but only to a degree. MacGyver's challenge is <i>picking</i> the right combination of random objects to do the job, even though individually it generally seems as though they really shouldn't. The way the Charmset facilitates this sort of thing is largely by giving us a big toolbox full of Awesome-but-(often <i>wildly</i>)-Impractical random shit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I guess all I can really say is that I disagree. &quot;Generally applicable&quot; is the sticking point really; a version of the Sidereals that <i>doesn't</i> force the Sids (and by extension their players) to employ a degree of lateral thinking to solve their problems is a version that completely loses my interest.<br /> <br /> Also, one must remember that even if they somehow find themselves without a single Charm applicable to the situation, a Sidereal's still no less capable than a heroic mortal, and this is supposedly the edition to finally terminate the tradition of mortals-can't-do-shit. At the end of the day, you can get a whole lot of general utility out of just, y'know, <i>being human</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">...also also, apparently italics are my new semicolons.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> These issues are exactly why I stressed on the two charm types that synergize with each other :<br /> <br /> - you can't just give a lots of impractical charms for each situation like MacGuyver gets a lot of random objects to tinker with. Because it would make their trees a mess and also because each charm costs just as much so having to buy multiple charms just to have tools for a few situations means character development will be way slower for sids. Creating once again a frustrating power gap.<br /> <br /> - the solution is to make charms that cover a wide set of situations , or flexible or that can be stunted towards different outcomes. And because of that, those charms can't be &quot;powerfull&quot; at the same time or they would be unbalanced (think BotBM : boosting all MA rolls and static values, providing an enhanced dice cap AND lasting a scene)<br /> <br /> - on the other hand you can't just make trees only with flexible but &quot;weak&quot; charms. It would be just like going to war with a multi-tool knife, a first aid kit but no rifle. Sure you can do a lot of things but you'll lack raw firepower. That's when the narrow but strong charms come in : they allow for strong thematic impacts and particularily reward you if you manage to manipulate the situation to fit the restriced use cases the charm works in.<br /> <br /> The end result is you deal with each situation by fiting them into patterns specific to each ability/constelation.<br /> <br /> For instance I have though of a verison of cash and murder games where you don't just wish to craft a relationship and pays the mote and magicaly create it. But instead he would need to create a situation where everyone else acknowledges the relationship and the target would become forced by fate (or peer pressure or whatever) to fit into the pattern. Of course to counterbalance the required efforts compared to the original charm, the created relationship would be stronger than &quot;pay a few willpowers to break it&quot;.<br /> <br /> Exemple : you want lady [x] to marry with the king. you disguise as her and seduce the king and convince him to get married. The day of the ceremony you arrange for the real lady [x] to be present and activate the charm so she feels a strong pull forcing her to wear the dress, accept the marriage, and live the rest of her life just as if she lived the moments with the king when it was actually someone else posing as her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T08:30:17-07:00","id":260612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cenobite451</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=260537#post260537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;There's always an Arquillian Battle Cruiser, or a Corillian Death Ray, or an intergalactic plague that is about to wipe out all life on this miserable little planet, and the only way these people can get on with their happy lives is that they Do. Not. Know about it!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's clever, putting together a setting that makes you root for the Thought Police.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T08:44:47-07:00","id":260615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack In The Box</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=260604#post260604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For instance I have though of a verison of cash and murder games where you don't just wish to craft a relationship and pays the mote and magicaly create it. But instead he would need to create a situation where everyone else acknowledges the relationship and the target would become forced by fate (or peer pressure or whatever) to fit into the pattern. Of course to counterbalance the required efforts compared to the original charm, the created relationship would be stronger than &quot;pay a few willpowers to break it&quot;.<br /> <br /> Exemple : you want lady [x] to marry with the king. you disguise as her and seduce the king and convince him to get married. The day of the ceremony you arrange for the real lady [x] to be present and activate the charm so she feels a strong pull forcing her to wear the dress, accept the marriage, and live the rest of her life just as if she lived the moments with the king when it was actually someone else posing as her.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to be how Charms in general are going to work going forward. No more of the &quot;I talk to a couple merchants once about how it's nice to give food to beggars, pay the cost, and inflict the whole kingdom with TID that makes them be nice to the homeless.&quot; Macro magic like that doesn't evoke the desired feeling of &quot;epic heroism arising from your puissance and effort instead of being just some power you sling and walk away from,&quot; and such a self-fulfilling nature is incredibly impersonal and dissonant to basically any real-world myth.<br /> <br /> So I bet the real Cash &amp; Murder Games will be closer to your idea, at least in what practical actions are needed to trigger it, than to the very-prevalent-in-2e &quot;Charm as actor&quot; model.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T09:20:12-07:00","id":260653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=260533#post260533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And on the other end of that, End Debate/Force Decision worry me a little in terms of story trivializing, though this is more of a 2e perspective. I think the 3e Intimacy mechanics should make it such that a Sidereal using Force Decision doesn't casually get to overwrite the Defining Intimacy of Capulet hating the Montagues, because 3e Charm theory and so on and so forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have to be that easy in 2nd edition.<br /> Neither End Debate nor Force Decision would change Motivations that have helped to perpetuate the conflict, if you've got an Oberyn Martell type character in the mix he'll play nicely for a while but if the other house doesn't give him the murderer's head on a silver plate he'll cause trouble eventually and obviously if it's a bitter feud he won't be the only squeaky wheel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T11:41:42-07:00","id":260805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=260533#post260533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, Venus has some very interesting views on what love is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's not all the Lovers. Even then, co-dependence and exploitation still doesn't necessarily mean people who bicker at one another and constantly misunderstand or explode over trivial slights, and then realise it's actually because they're really in love.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My kind of &quot;ideal&quot; Sidereal &quot;mundane&quot; mission is kinda like Romeo &amp; Juliet.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Cave of Two Lovers!<br /> <br /> Then you also get to have somebody perform the Secret Tunnel song.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And on the other end of that, End Debate/Force Decision worry me a little in terms of story trivializing, though this is more of a 2e perspective. I think the 3e Intimacy mechanics should make it such that a Sidereal using Force Decision doesn't casually get to overwrite the Defining Intimacy of Capulet hating the Montagues, because 3e Charm theory and so on and so forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can Force Decision do that? I mean, if a Capulet is already giving consideration to dropping the feud and making a deliberate effort to change, and even then you'd need somebody who isn't changeable or easily slighted so that they actually stick to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T12:14:19-07:00","id":260844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/257414-does-anybody-have-any-complains-about-sidereal-charms?p=260612#post260612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's clever, putting together a setting that makes you root for the Thought Police.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not <i> exactly</i> how I'd characterize them, but yes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/471-cenobite451","name":"Cenobite451","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar471_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T12:22:02-07:00","id":260849,"title":"","content":"I've always wanted a bit more Adjustment Bureau in my Sidereals, a little more care for the course of history by making the smallest adjustments necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T19:01:46-07:00","id":261069,"title":"","content":"1e's Force Decision, in addition to being irresistible and nearly infallible, was hugely unclear about what it did or what its limitations were, which was a serious problem with it. It was one of the worst charms in their set for that reason alone, and <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zaraborgstrom/ForceDecision\" target=\"_blank\">Moran's explanation of how it was meant to operate</a> was hard to read out of the text.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, 1e's End Debate is great and I love it. If I could have one charm in real life, End Debate would be on the shortlist. It's a short-circuit for bikeshedding or haggling, in essence -- if something needs to be decided, it goes to a binding unspoken vote with no further discussion. It completely ends a runaway bureaucratic process, and can permanently stymie a single corrupt official. Given that it requires an obvious dramatic flourish and is expensive enough that it can't be used at-will, I don't know how that's not narratively awesome?<br /> <br /> I mean, the way End Debate works is that you're having these long, argumentative diplomatic negotiations between villains hiding their antagonism behind a smile, and people with hopelessly irreconcilable differences, and you just shove back your chair and stand up all &quot;FUCK THIS&quot; and throw down this prayer strip like a firebomb (optionally with a Phoenix Wright Cornered denunciation), and that's the end of that. Its main use is to instantly end an engagement that would otherwise be draggy and unproductive, to cut the Gordian knot of Kafkaesque bureaucracy. It's very good for circumventing things that wouldn't be fun <i>anyway</i>, in other words, but using it outside those situations it doesn't do that much that can't already be done with lower-level Performance and Bureaucracy charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 09-19-2014, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}